diagnostics/builtin-shadowing/main.em:10:7: warning: `random` hides Emerald's built-in `random`
  const random = 4
        ^^^^^^
A name the program declares always wins, so `random` here means this one. Write `Emerald.random` to reach the built-in, or choose a different name.
diagnostics/builtin-shadowing/main.em:18:7: `Emerald.print` is built in, and built-in functions cannot be used as values
  print(Emerald.print)
        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Call it with parentheses, as in `Emerald.print(...)`, or wrap it in a lambda such as `{ value => Emerald.print(value) }`.
